    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the normal to the curve, in general form:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2-5x-5$ where $x=-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x-9y+83=0$",
          "worked": "Point of tangency:\n$$\\begin{align*}y_1&=f(-2)\\\\&=(-2)^2-5(-2)-5\\\\&=9\\end{align*}$$\nGradient function and tangent gradient:\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=2x-5\\\\m&=f'(-2)\\\\&=2(-2)-5\\\\&=-9\\end{align*}$$\nGradient of the normal:\n$$m_{\\perp}=-\\frac{1}{-9}=\\frac19.$$\nEquation of the normal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-y_1&=m_{\\perp}(x-x_1)\\\\y-9&=\\frac19(x+2)\\\\9y-81&=x+2\\\\x-9y+83&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=x^4-2x^3+4x+1$ where $x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x+2y-9=0$",
          "worked": "Point of tangency:\n$$\\begin{align*}y_1&=1^4-2(1)^3+4(1)+1\\\\&=4\\end{align*}$$\nGradient function and tangent gradient:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=4x^3-6x^2+4\\\\m&=4(1)^3-6(1)^2+4\\\\&=2\\end{align*}$$\nGradient of the normal:\n$$m_{\\perp}=-\\frac12.$$\nEquation of the normal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-y_1&=m_{\\perp}(x-x_1)\\\\y-4&=-\\frac12(x-1)\\\\2y-8&=-x+1\\\\x+2y-9&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
